  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The development would by reason of its change in use from class from Class C4 to Sui Generis would result in a material change of use whilst also increasing the intensity of the use of site in terms of noise and disturbance, coming and goings, increase waste, potential parking issues, potential for an increase in occupiers due to provision of large double bedrooms. The change from 6-person to 8-person would also result in the loss of a family sized unit as the unit would no longer be able to interchange uses between C3 and C4 under Part L of the GPDO. The change of use from a small HMO (Class C4) to a Large HMO (Sui Generis) does not fall under permitted development and the increase is considered a material change under The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended),  Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended) and Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015."
  ],
